Parity scope (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing): the web <Delta> is a PURE presentational leaf — its
only inputs are props + the display-boundary facades (useTranslation / useUnits / useFormatting via the
inline useUnitLabels). It has exactly THREE render branches: loading (skeleton), empty (missing/non-finite
current|previous -> em-dash), value (arrow + percent/absolute/both + comparedTo). It has NO error / stale /
offline branch — there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from. Reproducing those generic
states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so they are documented N/A, not skipped —
exactly as the sibling presentational primitives MetricCard (0095) and BatteryDelta (0077) did. All three
real branches + every sub-branch (percent/absolute/both, previous==0 -> "—", non-finite guard, hideArrow,
inline vs row, sm/md, currency prefix, efficiency-unit flip, precision precedence, colour precedence) are
reproduced and verified.

